      "content": "It's like you're just going through the motions, trying to keep the machine running, but it's all just a hollow imitation of life. You're not even sure what's left of you anymore, just a faint echo of a person who used to have a purpose. It's exhausting, not just physically, but emotionally too. You're just holding on out of habit, out of obligation, but not out of any real desire to keep going.",
